  "title": {
    "text": "Since the financial crisis, job churn has run about a fifth below its 2004 level, while productivity growth slowed",
    "subtitle": [
      "UK, index (2004 = 100). In 2004 the reallocation rate was 35.9% and real GVA per hour \u00a336 (2022 prices).",
      "Northern Ireland excluded (job flows from 2011). 2010 and 2023 are known spikes in the business register data.",
      "Sources: ONS Longitudinal Business Database (Secure Access, SN 9501); ONS Subregional productivity (June 2025); authors' calculations."
    ]
  },
